data: {"level":2,"reviewed":{"level":2,"label":"formula / approach","text":"With `z = X @ w`, `s = sigmoid(z)` and `n` rows, the gradient is\n`(2/n) * X.T @ ((s - y) * s * (1 - s))`. Two details matter. First, compute the sigmoid from\n`e = exp(-abs(z))`, so that no exponent is ever large and positive. Second, the local derivative\n`s (1 - s)` equals `e / (1 + e)**2`, which keeps its digits when `s` is close to 1."},"hints_note":null}

